{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Or it is made known to him.</b> Scripture holds a brief path, like 'to the priest' [i.e., a shortened construction]. The meaning is that the nasi either knows of his own accord that he sinned, or another person who saw him informs him. Grammatical analysis: הודע אליו is a past-tense verb, like והצר לך, and the one who informs is omitted, like אשר ילדה אותה ללוי. Rabbi Moses the Kohen says it belongs to the binyan whose agent is not named, for the cholam and shurek interchange, and its pattern is like ויוסף, הורד מצרימה. And the nasi shall bring a male goat because it is a זרזיר מתנים [a nimble-limbed he-goat], or a young buck, according to the interpretation of the Gaon [Saadia] in the book of Proverbs. It is a male because of the nasi's rank — only its blood is not brought inside the sanctuary, and the priests eat the nasi's sin-offering to make atonement on his behalf, for so it is written: 'And the high priest shall not eat his sin-offering.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:40.517055249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}